{
 "_doc": "Measured on the source crop the model was conditioned on (models_raw/<id>.source.png, 1024 px), pixel coords (x right, y down). wheels: name, hub_px (hub or axle box centre), rim_px (tyre edge points); back-projected onto the mesh for axle positions and diameters. nose_px: a pixel on the nose (+X). scale: a real distance between two named wheels sets the scale instead of height_m. level: 'wheels' levels the chassis on the measured wheel bottoms, 'body' (default above one tile) on the body itself (narrowest yaw, principal axis in side view). rail: 'lowest' puts the rail plane at the mesh's lowest point instead of under the wheels. color_px: boxes [x0, y0, x1, y1] whose median colour paints built wheels (small stock). inner_y: share of the half width inside which the model survives when its wheels are cut. Final-frame entries (metres from the part's centre, + towards the nose; heights above the rail): cut_boxes remove the model's running gear below top; cut_wheels remove named wheels outboard of inner_y; baked builds running gear rigid with the body sprite (a bogies.json-style spec, axles may name a measured wheel); bogies are the train's own bogie sprites, rolling/bogie_<style>_f<f>: bogie index of the part hangs at its pivot, which src/data pivots put where the image has the truck (the log prints them; at = 'image' draws it away from its pivot with bogieDraw instead), built from a spec or taken from the model's own truck (mesh box, squared up); attach boxes move end gear from the body onto that bogie, so it turns with it (pilots, couplers, steps of a rigid body on two or more trucks). symmetric (default true) rebuilds the side the source hides as the mirror of the seen one. detaper: parts whose box body is made equally wide along its length (the source's perspective leaves the near end wider).",
